#title Wasted Years
#author Iron Maiden
#category Piosenki zagraniczne

#verse
From the coast of gold, across the seven seas ~ e D
I'm travelin' on, far and wide ~ e D
But now it seems, I'm just a stranger to myself ~ C D e
And all the things I sometimes do, it isn't me but someone else ~ D C

#verse
I close my eyes and think of home ~ e D
Another city goes by in the night ~ e D
Ain't it funny how it is? You never miss it till it's gone away ~ C D e
And my heart is lying there and will be till my dying day ~ D C

#chorus
So, understand ~ G C A D C A
Don't waste your time always searching for those wasted years ~ e D C
Face up, make your stand ~ G C A D C A
And realize you're living in the golden years ~ e D C

#verse
Too much time on my hands, I got you on my mind ~ e D
Can't ease this pain, so easily ~ e D
When you can't find the words to say ~ C
It's hard to make it through another day ~ D e
And it makes me wanna cry, and throw my hands up to the sky ~ D C

#chorus
So, understand ~ G C A D C A
Don't waste your time always searching for those wasted years ~ e D C
Face up, make your stand ~ G C A D C A
And realize you're living in the golden years ~ e D C

